  "body": "The officer home page used an unstyled list for My profile, leaving the details cramped at the left of a wide card. Reuse the existing profile stats grid so the four fields align on desktop and stack on phones. This changes only `app/views/home/index.html.erb`.\n\n## Associated User Story\n\n[P5-31: Add details to signup](https://pt-502.atlassian.net/browse/P5-31)\n\nAs a user, I want to also be able to add expected graduation, PT school application (put ‘anticipated application cycle’) - (summers only, for example summer 2026, summer 2027, etc…), show availability for carpooling for field trips, and opt into providing a phone number.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n### Members can add and edit these profile details, and the phone number is only shared if they opt in.\n\n- Sunny: A member opens their profile and selects an expected graduation term, a PT school application summer (e.g., Summer 2026, Summer 2027), whether they're available to carpool, and optionally checks a box to share their phone number and enters it. They save and see a confirmation. The information appears on their profile, carpool availability is visible to officers when planning field trips, and the phone number is visible only if they opted in.\n- Rainy: A member leaves a required field blank, picks a non-summer application term, enters an invalid phone number, or the save fails. The system shows a clear error (e.g., \"Please choose a summer term\" or \"Enter a valid phone number\") instead of failing silently, and their previous information stays in place. If a member has not opted in, their phone number is never shown to others, and only the member and officers can edit their own details.\n\nDefinition of Done -\n\nA story is done when its acceptance criteria are met and every item in the team PR template is satisfied:\n(A) code review by a non-author, coding standard met, RuboCop checked with output/CI link, and setup changes documented;\n(B) the human-only maintainability checks (meaningful comments and names, skinny controllers, thin views, DRY, Rails conventions, foreign keys, enums, nested routes);\n(C) tests added or updated and passing. Any deferred items or RuboCop exclusions are explained in Section D of the PR.\n\n## Validation and Setup\n\n338 RSpec examples, 0 failures, 1 existing pending example. RuboCop: 124 files, no offenses. Visually checked the officer dashboard on desktop and at 390px width; the profile fields stack without clipping.\n\nNo setup changes or migrations.\n\n## Section D: Deferred Items\n\nNon-author review is pending. The existing pending HomeHelper example is unchanged. No new RuboCop exclusions.\n",
